<!--
    What may leave this device: nothing.

    `android:allowBackup="false"` turns off the *cloud* backup and nothing
    else. Since API 31, transferring app data to a new device during its setup
    is a separate mode, allowed until these rules say otherwise — so until this
    file existed the manifest claimed more than it did (#110).

    The decision behind it, taken 2026-09-20: the case being solved is
    reinstalling on the *same* device, which is #96 and nothing else. Carrying
    a library to a new tablet may become a task later, and allowing it then
    means deleting the excludes below on purpose, rather than discovering that
    it had been on all along.

    Three things that are not obvious, and were checked rather than reasoned:

    * A missing section means that mode is *fully enabled*, not off. Leaving
      `<device-transfer>` out is what the app did until now.
    * `domain="root"` does not stand for the rest. Each domain is walked
      separately, files/, databases/ and shared_prefs/ are filtered out of the
      root walk (`BackupAgent.onFullBackup`), and `external` is not under the
      app's private root at all. Hence all nine.
    * `path` is optional. Absent, it defaults to the empty string, which is the
      whole domain directory (`FullBackup.parseRules`).

    `<cloud-backup>` is deliberately absent: `allowBackup="false"` already
    covers it, and this app is not in Google's backup at all (checked with
    `dumpsys backup` on the tablet). `<cross-platform-transfer>` (API 36.1, to
    iOS) is opt-in — it takes a `platform` and the bundle id of a counterpart
    app, and there is no such app — so there is nothing to exclude there.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
        <exclude domain="device_root" />
        <exclude domain="device_file" />
        <exclude domain="device_database" />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
